  "title": "A Contributor+ stored cross-site scripting (XSS) issue in the labels of the Comments Pagination and Post Navigation Link blocks",
  "summary": "The Comments Pagination Next, Comments Pagination Previous and Post Navigation Link blocks output their label without escaping, so a user with the Contributor role or above can store script in post content.\r\n\r\nWordPress 7.1.4 has been released containing a fix for the vulnerability, and as a courtesy to users on older branches the fix has been backported to all branches back to 5.9.\r\n\r\nDiscovered and responsibly disclosed by Alex Concha of the WordPress Security Team.",
